" hi's vim override, kept to the minimum that earns the `-u`: vim's own shipped
" defaults, so the alias is not a downgrade. Nothing to taste lives here - your own
" $_HI_CONFIG_DIR/vim.rc replaces this file wholesale.

" must be first: `vim -u <file>` implies 'compatible', which disables <> key
" notation and a good deal else. defaults.vim clears it too, but that file is
" not on every vim and never on neovim.
set nocompatible

" the out-of-the-box editor rather than the 1976 one, spelled the way vim
" itself spells it. `unlet!` because a system vimrc may have set the skip flag;
" `silent!` because neovim ships no such file and needs none.
unlet! skip_defaults_vim
silent! source $VIMRUNTIME/defaults.vim

" belt and braces for a vim old enough to have no defaults.vim; neovim has both
" on already, and setting them twice costs nothing.
syntax enable
filetype plugin indent on
  augroup END
endif
